\id PSA  
\h Psalms 
\toc1 PSALMS 
\toc2 Psalms 
\toc3 PSA 
\mt1 PSALMS  
\c 22  
\d (23) A Psalm of David.  
\q1
\v 1 The Lord tends me as a shepherd, and I shall lack nothing.   
\q1
\v 2 In a place of green grass, there he has made me dwell: he has nourished me by the water of rest.   
\q1
\v 3 He has restored my soul: he has guided me into the paths of righteousness, for his name's sake.   
\q1
\v 4 Yes, even if I should walk in the midst of the shadow of death, I will not be afraid of evils: for you are with me; your rod and your staff, these have comforted me.   
\q1
\v 5 You have prepared a table before me in presence of them that afflict me: you have thoroughly anointed my head with oil; and your cup cheers me like the best \add wine\add*.   
\q1
\v 6 Your mercy also shall follow me all the days of my life: and my dwelling \add shall be\add* in the house of the Lord for a very long time.   
\c 23  
\d (24) A Psalm for David on the first day of the week.  
\q1
\v 1 The earth is the Lord's and the fullness thereof; the world, and all that dwell in it.   
\q1
\v 2 He has founded it upon the seas, and prepared it upon the rivers.   
\q1
\v 3 Who shall go up to the mountain of the Lord, and who shall stand in his holy place?   
\q1
